$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Entry: 2; Yield: 100%. A mixture of m-xylene (4.0 mL), B2pin2 (91.3 mg,
359.5 μmol) and mBPV-MOF-Ir (5.0 mg, 0.1 mol% Ir) were charged into a
Schlenk tube. The tube was heated to reflux under nitrogen at 115 °C for
20 h. The solid catalyst was separated via centrifugation. The extract
was passed through a short plug of celite and then concentrated in vacuo.
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2- dioxaborolan-2-yl)-m-xylene in 98% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst prepared and used, arene was also used as
solvent, 97% isolated yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
