$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 142-82-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Entry: 18; Yield: 100%. In a glovebox, B2pin2 (18.3 mg, 71.9 μmol),
indole (17.1 mg, 143.5 μmol), n-heptane (4.0 mL), and mPT-MOF-Ir (5.0 mg,
0.5 mol % Ir) were charged into a Schlenk tube. The mixture was refluxed
under nitrogen at 115 °C in an oil bath for 3-4 h. During heating, the
solution was slowly stirred. After completion of the reaction, the
mixture was cooled to room temperature and the solid catalyst was
separated via centrifugation in the glovebox. All the volatiles of the
supernatant were removed in vacuo to give crude
2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2- dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole as a colorless
solid (isolated yield of crude product: 33.6 mg, 138.0 μmol, 96.2%; GC
yield: 97%), which was sufficiently pure as determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy (Figure S31). 4.0 mL solution of B2pin2 (18.3 mg, 71.9 μmol)
and indole (17.1 mg, 143.5 μmol) in m- xylene was added to the recovered
solid catalyst and then the mixture was transferred to the Schlenk tube.
After heating at 115 °C for 4 h, the solid catalyst was separated via
centrifugation in the glovebox. The volatiles of the supernatant was
removed in vacuo. 2-(4,4,5,5-
tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole (GC yield: 100%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, catalyst prepared and used, 94% isolated yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
