$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 3-bromobenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor was
charged with 3-bromobenzaldehyde (185.0 mg, 1.0 mmol), tBuNH2 (420.3 μL,
4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred for 4 h at room
temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced pressure. In a
glove box, this crude imine was charged with [Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg,
1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2
(177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M). The microreactor was
capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into pre-heated aluminum
block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h. After
completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced pressure and
chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as eluent). 305.0
mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde 3n (98%) as solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 9.98 (s, 1H), 8.20 (s, 1H), 8.16 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 8.09 (t,
J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 1.36 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 191.1, 143.3,
137.6, 135.5, 134.0, 123.5, 84.8, 25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 31.9.
HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C13H16BBrO3 [M+HCOO]- 355.0352, found 355.0351.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
