$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 2,3-dimethoxybenzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton
microreactor was charged with 2,3-dimethoxybenzaldehyde (166.2 mg, 1.0
mmol), tBuNH2 (420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and
stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried under
reduced pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25
μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M).
The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into
pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for
12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (chloroform as
eluent). 268.7 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde 3s (92%) as colourless
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.38 (s, 1H), 7.87 (s, 1H), 7.51 (s,
1H), 3.97 (s, 3H), 3.91 (s, 3H), 1.30 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 190.2, 154.8, 152.4, 129.2, 126.9, 123.5, 84.2, 62.2, 56.2, 24.9. 11B
NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 31.0. HRMS (ESI m/z calcd for C15H21BO5 [M+Na]+
315.1380, found 315.1375.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
