$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meta-borylation of 4-(benzyloxy)benzaldehyde: A 5.0 mL Weaton
microreactor was charged with 4-(benzyloxy)benzaldehyde (212.2 mg, 1.0
mmol), MeNH2 (10.0 equiv) and dry dichloromethane (3.0 mL) and stirred
for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried under reduced
pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), TMP (7.08 mg, 3.0 mol%), HBpin (7.25
μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv.) and dry THF (2.5 mL, 0.4M).
The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and placed into
pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for
12 h. After completion (judged by GC), THF was removed under reduced
pressure and chromatographic separation with silica gel (12%
ethylacetate/hexane as eluent). 300.1 mg of meta-borylated benzaldehyde
3i (89%) as white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.91 (s, 1H), 8.23
(d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.96 (dd, J = 8.4 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.59 (d, J =
7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.31-7.40 (m, 3H), 7.04 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (s, 2H),
1.38 (s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 191.3, 168.0, 140.1, 136.7,
134.2, 129.7, 128.6, 127.8, 126.8, 112.0, 84.1, 70.1, 25.1. 11B NMR (128
MHz, CDCl3): δ 33.6. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C20H23BO4 [M+H]+ 339.1689,
found 339.1692.
