$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Evaluation and optimization of reaction conditions: General Procedure: a
A 5.0 mL Weaton microreactor was charged with benzaldehyde (1a) (106.0
mg, 1.0 mmol), t BuNH2 (420.3 μL, 4.0 mmol) and dry dichloromethane (3.0
mL) and stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The crude mixture was dried
under reduced pressure. In a glove box, this crude imine was charged with
[Ir(cod)(OMe)]2 (10.0 mg, 1.5 mol%), appropriate amount of ligand (L1:
9.03 mg; 8-AQ: 4.32 mg, L2: 6.24 mg; L3: 3.24 mg; L4: 2.82 mg; 3.0 mol%),
HBpin (7.25 μL, 5.0 mol%), B2pin2 (177.8 mg, 0.7 equiv) and dry THF (2.5
mL, 0.4M). The microreactor was capped with a teflon pressure cap and
placed into pre-heated aluminum block at 90°C. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 12 h and the results are summarized in the above table.
ortho-borylated product. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.54 (s, 1H), 7.95
(d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.85 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.54-7.61 (m, 3H), 1.39
(s, 12H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 194.8, 141.4, 135.6, 133.1, 130.9,
128.0, 84.6, 25.0. 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 33.5. HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd
for C13H17BO3 [M+Na]+ 255.1168, found 255.1159.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, optimization study (reagent, ligand, stoichiometry,
B-source)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formal Ir-Catalyzed Ligand-Enabled Ortho and Meta Borylation of Aromatic
Aldehydes via in Situ-Generated Imines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bisht, Ranjana; Chattopadhyay, Buddhadeb
